@startuml
title Keyspace Commands - Redis-like Server

' DEL, EXISTS, KEYS, TYPE, DBSIZE and FLUSHDB against the keyspace. All run on
' the keyspace thread, so none races another. A key past its deadline is
' removed lazily only by a lookup (find); DEL, KEYS and DBSIZE do not look
' it up, which is bug #40 (docs/features/key_expiry/README.md).

start
:Command arrives, arity already checked;

switch (Command?)
case ( DEL k1 k2 ... )
  :removed = 0;
  repeat
    :erase(key): drop its deadline, then its value
    (no deadline check first);
    if (Key was in the table?) then (yes)
      :removed++;
    endif
  repeat while (More keys?) is (yes)
  :Reply ":<removed>";
  note right
    A key past its deadline that the sweep has not
    reached is still in the table, so DEL counts it
    and replies :1, though GET, EXISTS and TYPE
    already see it as missing.
  end note
case ( EXISTS k1 k2 ... )
  :count = 0;
  repeat
    :contains(key), which is find(key);
    if (Key past its deadline?) then (yes)
      :Erase it and its deadline, expired_keys++;
      :Not counted;
    elseif (Key in the table?) then (yes)
      :count++;
    else (no)
      :Not counted;
    endif
  repeat while (More keys?) is (yes)
  :Reply ":<count>"
  (a key named twice counts twice);
case ( TYPE key )
  :find(key), removing it first if past its deadline;
  if (Key found?) then (yes)
    :Reply "+string", "+list", "+hash" or "+set";
  else (no)
    :Reply "+none";
  endif
case ( KEYS pattern )
  :Walk every key in the table;
  if (Key past its deadline?) then (yes)
    :Skip it (not removed, not matched);
  elseif (glob_match(pattern, key)?) then (yes)
    :Collect it;
  else (no)
    :Skip it;
  endif
  :Reply with the collected keys as an array of bulk strings
  (empty array if none match, order undefined);
  note right
    Visits every key and holds the keyspace thread
    meanwhile, so other clients wait.
  end note
case ( DBSIZE )
  :Reply ":<number of keys in the table>";
  note right
    Counts keys past their deadline that
    nothing has removed yet.
  end note
case ( FLUSHDB, with or without arguments )
  :clear(): drop every value,
  every deadline and the deadline index;
  :Reply "+OK";
  note right
    expired_keys is not changed:
    nothing here expired.
  end note
endswitch

stop
@enduml
